This work presents a band structure calculation for a twisted bilayer Boron Nitride supercell using a full tight-binding model. The code used for this calculation includes:

1:band.py: This is the input file for the tight-binding calculation, based on the QUEST model.

2:tB/tN/bB/bN: These files contain the coordinates of the top layer Boron atoms, top layer Nitrid atoms, bottom layer Boron atoms, and bottom Nitrid atoms.

3:onsite: This file contains the onsite energy for each atom.

4:eigvals_on: This file contains the output eigenvalues of the band structures.

5:plot_band.py: This code is used to plot the band structure using the eigenvalue data.

Note that the QUEST code will be made public at a later time.


